window.OPOSSUM_FOOT_LEGAL_HTML = "<h3>Who owns this</h3>\n<p>Opossum Foot — the app, the name, the logo, the design, and everything in it — is the property of <strong>Opossum Foot LLC</strong>, an Iowa limited liability company. Copyright © 2026 Opossum Foot LLC. All rights reserved.</p>\n<h3>Closed beta — keep it in the circle</h3>\n<p>You're using a closed beta, and the circle is small on purpose. Please don't share the beta link, copy the app, or pull it apart to build your own version of it. If someone wants in, point them at Tanner.</p>\n<h3>No warranties</h3>\n<p>The app is provided as-is. It was built to be solid, but no software is perfect — Opossum Foot LLC isn't responsible for anything that goes wrong because of a glitch. Back up your data in Settings — the full JSON backup is the one that restores everything; the CSV exports are your spreadsheet copies.</p>\n<h3>Seasons are reminders, not law</h3>\n<p>Season dates, bag limits, and everything else in the Seasons tab are reminders only — <strong>not legal authority</strong>. Always verify with your state agency and local ordinances before you trap. Nothing in this app decides whether trapping is legal today.</p>\n<h3>The fine print, plainly</h3>\n<p>This isn't legal advice, and it isn't the full terms of service — those are coming. By using the beta, you agree to use it legally and to keep the beta link to yourself.</p>";
